--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modifications
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`review-standards-spec` is upstream's `code-review` skill, renamed.

Claude Code ships a built-in `/code-review` — the one that takes `ultra`, `--fix`,
`--comment` and a PR number. Installing upstream's skill under its own name shadows
that built-in, replacing a documented workflow with a different tool that answers a
different question. Renaming keeps both reachable: the built-in hunts correctness
bugs in a diff; this one checks a diff against a repo's documented standards and
against the ticket it came from.

The rename touches three things — the skill's directory, its frontmatter `name`,
and every sibling that calls it. `implement` and `tdd` are modified for that reason
alone: one reference each, retargeted from `code-review` to `review-standards-spec`.
Their substance is upstream's, unchanged.

Upstream also ships `ask-matt`, which calls `code-review` and would need the same
edit. It is not a dispatch dependency and is not redistributed here.

If you want the upstream skills unmodified, take them from the source above. This
repository does not attempt to track it: no upstream commit is pinned, and the
copies here will drift as Matt changes his.
